#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059482 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059653 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f372d875-4de9-5ed1-86a6-80ceeddd3fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of a Triangle's Side Using the Law of Cosines"}] :question/id #uuid "0383d558-2227-5c47-b0d3-8ac48c7b1e7a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3286" :question/problem "Consider the following triangle:\n\n![](images/9f/9fbf9672296b128a16336120999c2c836d950fda32154bc7a0f0a91b0e8799e6.png)\n\nCalculate the length of the side $a$, giving your answer to the nearest tenth." :question/worked-solution "The Law of Cosines states that\n\n$$\na^2 = b^2+c^2-2bc\\cos{A}\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nm\\angle A = 75^{\\circ},\\quad b = 10,\\quad c=9\n$$\n\nSubstituting the numbers into the formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na^{2} &= 10^{2} + 9^{2} - 2(10)(9)\\cos 75^{∘} \\\\\n&= 100 + 81 - 180\\cos 75^{∘} \\\\\n&= 181 - 180 \\cdot 0.2588… \\\\\n&= 181 - 46.5874… \\\\\n&= 134.4126\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places\n\nTaking the square root gives\n\n$$\na = \\sqrt{134.4126} = 11.6\n$$\n\nto the nearest tenth."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059483 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8da5ae4c-c94c-5a8c-ba62-5df6e500008a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Measure of an Angle in a Triangle Using the Law of Cosines"}] :question/id #uuid "84630f24-0d62-5ab3-8f9d-e03e815820cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-3288" :question/problem "Consider the following triangle:\n\n![](images/e0/e03942073ddfd8672fe5c5e4bd7bc81f0dc22f8682e3a364b001c280b315e721.png)\n\nCalculate the measure of the angle $\\angle A$ to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "We use the Law of Cosines to solve for angle $A$:\n\n$$\n\\cos A = \\frac{b^{2} + c^{2} - a^{2}}{2bc}\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\na=9,\\quad b=7,\\quad c=12\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos A &= (7^{2} + 12^{2} - 9^{2})/(2(7)(12)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{49 + 144 - 81}{168} \\\\\n&= \\frac{112}{168} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠A &= \\arccos (\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\\n&= 48.19^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059653 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f372d875-4de9-5ed1-86a6-80ceeddd3fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of a Triangle's Side Using the Law of Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2363919f-7752-5ca9-81ef-e4fd3d83132e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569491} {:answer/id #uuid "309e10fe-5899-53fa-abb8-cefdf02e6c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569513} {:answer/id #uuid "743ab8f6-0462-5ecf-ade3-7484e3a5260d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569635} {:answer/id #uuid "780e6ca6-bcc8-586b-a1a2-2c6f926a90aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569643} {:answer/id #uuid "f076441a-3c72-578b-a6a9-77ba9855c9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "743ab8f6-0462-5ecf-ade3-7484e3a5260d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569635} :answer-field/id #uuid "c88c1875-f160-569e-9282-5ba3baa13df9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b48e833b-67d8-59d3-81e1-297aecf64a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-14692" :question/problem "![](images/66/66d24d8cc70ffaed2421d0a5a0086fd7848b4d3e98bc8a6e87588c6c2b04e19d.png)\n\nCalculate the length of the side $c$, giving your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The Law of Cosines states that\n\n$$\n{c}^{2}={a}^{2}+{b}^{2}-2ab\\operatorname{cos}⁡C.\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nm∠C={43}^{∘},\\,a=10,\\,b=13.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the numbers into the formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}^{2} & ={10}^{2}+{13}^{2}-2(10)(13)\\operatorname{cos}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =100+169-260\\operatorname{cos}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =269-260(0.731\\,35…) \\\\  & =269-190.151\\,96 \\\\  & =78.848\\,04.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places\n\nTaking the square root gives\n\n$$\nc=\\sqrt{78.848\\,04}=8.88\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8da5ae4c-c94c-5a8c-ba62-5df6e500008a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Measure of an Angle in a Triangle Using the Law of Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183e7e96-ee7e-5850-a1bf-75f30a215f0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{39.81}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569480} {:answer/id #uuid "5a328bb2-83f5-57f5-b38d-f472331c7c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{33.56}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569573} {:answer/id #uuid "6c4ac95c-8556-5fbf-965a-0eb4c8e0345a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{36.44}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569616} {:answer/id #uuid "84465da0-5d9b-563a-a817-64751d321a8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{44.26}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569661} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7753a4-af15-5a0d-94f5-f6eecf8f7ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{28.18}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a328bb2-83f5-57f5-b38d-f472331c7c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{33.56}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569573} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f77438e-6a65-5147-9492-745b947b2082" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ede5978-9720-5b14-aefb-d172677e353f" :question/math-academy-id "q-14701" :question/problem "![](images/40/40ee0a065e8733bd1ab22c04af39b358da5106791af6b99017cef1d07c13abcd.png)\n\nFor the triangle above, find $m∠A$ in degrees to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "We use the Law of Cosines to solve for angle $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡A &=\\frac{{b}^{2}+{c}^{2}-{a}^{2}}{2bc}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\na=5,\\,b=8,\\,c=9.\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡A & =\\frac{{9}^{2}+{8}^{2}-{5}^{2}}{2(9)(8)} \\\\  & =\\frac{81+64-25}{144} \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{144} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{5}{6}) \\\\  & ={33.56}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8da5ae4c-c94c-5a8c-ba62-5df6e500008a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Measure of an Angle in a Triangle Using the Law of Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05ee243d-a0f6-58ea-a3e3-0cc51073be09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{27.42}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569454} {:answer/id #uuid "6fa4e6b5-7b61-5d05-8391-af677ab50fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{26.38}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569624} {:answer/id #uuid "88480d0d-769a-530a-9275-5454a6d74513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{23.62}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569668} {:answer/id #uuid "9914af0e-f526-50f6-98f8-1152e4ec30ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{20.73}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569688} {:answer/id #uuid "dcd7adc3-cc26-59cb-97d3-e0576be8c6d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{29.38}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fa4e6b5-7b61-5d05-8391-af677ab50fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{26.38}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569624} :answer-field/id #uuid "264c3506-720d-5be8-870e-eb9352af9f27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39fc3bcb-e781-5ee0-b172-9c69c7f5c440" :question/math-academy-id "q-201" :question/problem "A triangle has sides $a$, $b$, and $c.$ The sides $a$, $b$, and $c$ are of lengths  $9$, $12$, and $18$, respectively. What is the measure of the angle between the sides $b$ and $c?$ Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The following triangle illustrates the information given.\n\n![](images/de/dede0326d992509dedf1c3a2854b47076ccc48ebf0e07705c8c12762d8ecdead.png)\n\nWe use the Law of Cosines to solve for angle $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡A & =\\frac{{b}^{2}+{c}^{2}-{a}^{2}}{2bc}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\na=9,\\,b=12,\\,c=18.\n$$\n\nThis gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡A & =\\frac{{12}^{2}+{18}^{2}-{9}^{2}}{2(12)(18)} \\\\  & =\\frac{144+324-81}{432} \\\\  & =\\frac{387}{432}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠F & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{387}{432}) \\\\  & ={26.38}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059653 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f372d875-4de9-5ed1-86a6-80ceeddd3fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of a Triangle's Side Using the Law of Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60afb59e-20de-5529-866a-21d64ca9864f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20.19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569592} {:answer/id #uuid "9c9dd926-9dc5-5342-8887-1c800d75fce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569693} {:answer/id #uuid "b6227353-fd1f-588c-87c0-4d2fbcb0ec82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569733} {:answer/id #uuid "b89436fa-8ee2-59d5-8e46-dec0a28c1f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19.80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569736} {:answer/id #uuid "efac4f0d-dc62-5b54-bc2c-d45e89767fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c9dd926-9dc5-5342-8887-1c800d75fce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569693} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bbe43c0-91be-5bd2-8a68-52cc63b578a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "903d6591-71d0-55aa-98cb-3913a9cd46ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-6409" :question/problem "![](images/43/43a50373c9cfa5925a01054ab5eb465ac8a6220fced41ab46d8e026908884537.png)\n\nCalculate the length of the side $x$, giving your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The Law of Cosines states that\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}={y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡X.\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nm∠X={66}^{∘},\\,y=16,\\,z=19.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the numbers into the formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & ={16}^{2}+{19}^{2}-2(16)(19)\\operatorname{cos}⁡{66}^{∘} \\\\  & =256+361-608\\operatorname{cos}⁡{66}^{∘} \\\\  & =617-608(0.406\\,73…) \\\\  & =617-247.295\\,88 \\\\  & =369.704\\,12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places\n\nTaking the square root gives\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{369.708\\,16}=19.23\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}]}
